maritime-edge — LICENSING MAP

This repository is multi-licensed by directory. There is no single license
covering the whole tree. Full license texts are in LICENSES/.

  PATH                     LICENSE                        SPDX
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  scripts/                 Non-Commercial Research-Only,  LicenseRef-Argus-
    (except analysis/)     No Derivatives, v1.3           NCND-1.3

  scripts/analysis/        GNU Affero GPL v3.0            AGPL-3.0-only

  docs/                    CC Attribution-NonCommercial-  CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0
                           NoDerivatives 4.0 Intl

  root files               LicenseRef-Argus-NCND-1.3      (see below)
  (README, requirements.txt, .gitignore)

A LICENSE file inside a directory overrides this map for files beneath it.
Every source file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier header stating its
license; the header is authoritative for that file.


WHY scripts/analysis/ IS SEPARATE

chroma_sweep.py imports Ultralytics YOLO, which is licensed AGPL-3.0. The
Ultralytics authors assert that importing the package creates a combined work
subject to the AGPL. That reading is contested for Python imports but is
enforced in practice, so this repository treats it as binding and isolates all
detector-importing code under scripts/analysis/ under the AGPL.

Code under scripts/ outside analysis/ does not import Ultralytics or any other
copyleft dependency. Dependencies run one direction only: scripts/analysis/
may import from scripts/; scripts/ must not import from scripts/analysis/.


